{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794463300,"nonce":"gORx5ljjptUSmL8in7C0V3qq6Mw=","title":"x","message":"The build library's push Step uses run_as_root because crane:debug is uid 0 and Steps can't set a uid. It is self-service (all capabilities dropped, no privilege escalation, RuntimeDefault seccomp), but Policy input shows grants: [\"run-as-root\"], so an org Policy that denies root refuses every build.\nOptions: an image (our own, or a pinned crane variant) with a numeric non-root USER and a shell; or a run_as_user field for Steps. Found by the Fable review of #182.","files":null}]}